on_maps_2026-v1.2.0.zip", "size": 27453943, "checksum": "md5:8b44eadb8e81d7eaddd24b852081807b", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23706750/files/aortizm1/ortiz_dissertation_maps_2026-v1.2.0.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1913678"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 4, "unique_downloads": 4, "views": 25, "unique_views": 24, "version_downloads": 3, "version_unique_downloads": 3, "version_unique_views": 8, "version_views": 9}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-27T19:24:47.999173+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-27T19:24:48.198642+00:00", "id": 23700240, "conceptrecid": "22681257", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23700240", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22681257", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23700240", "metadata": {"title": "Replication Data and Code for: Does Scheduled Urban Water Rationing Increase Reported Domestic Violence? Evidence from Bogot\u00e1's Rotating Rationing Policy", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23700240", "publication_date": "2026-10-27", "description": "<p>This replication package accompanies &ldquo;Does Scheduled Urban Water Rationing Increase Reported Domestic Violence? Evidence from Bogot&aacute;&rsquo;s Rotating Rationing Policy&rdquo; by Natalia Galvis Arias.</p>\n<p>The study examines Bogot&aacute;&rsquo;s 2024&ndash;2025 rotating water-rationing programme using twelve hydraulic service polygons assigned to nine shifts and twenty shared hydraulic boundaries. The primary specification uses the operational 08:00&ndash;08:00 water-day clock.</p>\n<p>The package includes R analysis scripts, hydraulic geography and rationing-calendar inputs, analysis-ready aggregate count panels, a codebook, software requirements, replication instructions, numerical outputs, manuscript tables and figures, and manuscript source files.</p>\n<p>The default pipeline reproduces the statistical analyses from the included aggregate data. Four manually composed maps are supplied as static exhibits. Historical bandwidth selections are supplied as fixed inputs rather than re-estimated.</p>\n<p>Individual emergency-call records, incident coordinates and case identifiers are not included. Access to the underlying administrative records must be requested separately from Bogot&aacute;&rsquo;s Secretar&iacute;a Distrital de Seguridad, Convivencia y Justicia; instructions are provided in docs/DATA_ACCESS.md.</p>\n<p>The aggregate-input pipeline was independently executed successfully. All nine generated tables matched the supplied tables exactly, all 43 output CSVs agreed numerically within documented tolerances, and all 47 manuscript-value checks passed.</p>\n<p>Licensing: author-created aggregate data are designated CC BY 4.0; author-owned software code is licensed under the MIT License. Municipal source materials retain their original publisher terms. See LICENSE and the data-access documentation for details.</p>\n<p>Repository: <a href=\"https://github.com/nataliagalvisarias/Bogota_water_rationing_replication\">https://github.com/nataliagalvisarias/Bogota_water_rationing_replication</a><br>Version: 2.0.0</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Natalia Galvis Arias", "affiliation": "University of Manchester"}], "keywords": ["water rationing \u00b7 domestic violence \u00b7 Bogot\u00e1 \u00b7 urban economics \u00b7 infrastructure \u00b7 replication package \u00b7 spatial analysis"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/nataliagalvisarias/Bogota_water_rationing_replication", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "2.0.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/nataliagalvisarias/Bogota_water_rationing_replication", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "r", "title": {"en": "R"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_