/23630077/files/Replication%20package.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1964000"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 8, "unique_downloads": 7, "views": 96, "unique_views": 62, "version_downloads": 8, "version_unique_downloads": 7, "version_unique_views": 62, "version_views": 96}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-26T20:59:37.694845+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T21:20:16.023735+00:00", "id": 23675983, "conceptrecid": "23675982", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23675983", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23675982", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23675983", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Disembedding or Persistent Embeddedness? Testing Polanyi against Granovetter", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23675983", "publication_date": "2026-10-26", "description": "<p>Code and country-level derived data that reproduce the results of &ldquo;Disembedding or Persistent Embeddedness? Testing Polanyi against Granovetter.&rdquo; Python scripts build a respondent extract from the WVS Trend File 1981&ndash;2022 (v4.1) and the EVS Trend File 1981&ndash;2017 (ZA7503 v3.0.0), which users must download from the World Values Survey Association and GESIS under their own terms. They also build country-level files from the Fraser Institute EFW Panel Dataset (2026) and the OECD Social Expenditure Database. A Stata 19.5 do-file reproduces Tables 3 and 4 and Figure 2. The respondent-level survey data are not redistributed.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bayraktar, Murat", "affiliation": "\u0130stanbul Esenyurt \u00dcniversitesi", "orcid": "0000-0003-4028-192X"}], "keywords": ["embeddedness", "Karl Polanyi", "particularized trust", "double movement", "market institutions"], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23675982"}}]}