.23659454", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22137805", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23659454", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for: Toward Verifiable Literary Classrooms: Deterministic Corpus-Anchored Verification, Grounding, and In-Loop Repair for LLM Quotation Fidelity", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23659454", "publication_date": "2026-10-26", "description": "Frozen SHA256-anchored corpora, task and prompt files, the deterministic corpus-anchored verifier, the verification-repair harness, retrieval baselines, the audit-only guardrail, frozen run logs, the preregistration, the non-destructive locator-correction layer with its acceptance-check script, and the analysis scripts that regenerate every headline number, table, and figure in the article, including the GEE appendix with its exact analysis sample, the factor-level and equal-budget policy-mixing analyses, the quotation-length distribution audit, and the complete records of the 360-judgment two-judge three-evidence-condition experiment.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Guo, Ping", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Fan, Wei", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Yang, Jiaqiang", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Zhang, Guangqian", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["large language models", "quotation fidelity", "deterministic verification", "literary education", "reproducibility"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/fanwei110/verifiable-literary-classrooms/tree/v1.1.2", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v1.1.2", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/fanwei110/verifiable-literary-classrooms"}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 3, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22137805"}}]}, "notes": "If you use this replication package, please cite the accompanying IEEE Access article."}, "title": "Replication package for: Toward Verifiable Literary Classrooms: Deterministic Corpus-Anchored Verification, Grounding, and In-Loop Repair for LLM Quotation Fidelity", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23659454", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23659454?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23659454", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23659454", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23659454", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22137805", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22137805", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22137805", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22137805", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23659454/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23659454/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23659454/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/access", "communities": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/communities", "communities-suggestions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/communities-suggestions", "request_deletion": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/request-deletion", "file_modification": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/file-modification", "quota_increase": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/quota-increase", "requests": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/requests"}, "updated": "2026-10-26T07:31:29.021560+00:00", "recid": "23659454", "revision": 4, "files": [{"id": "4e433c72-56e6-420e-956b-8f2d3bbe69f1", "key": "fanwei110/verifiable-literary-classrooms-v1.1.2.zip", "size": 16624429, "checksum": "md5:38064da09f46878fc81e7b9c7bcc9f2e", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23659454/files/fanwei110/verifiable-literary-classrooms-v1.1.2.zip/content"}}], "swh": null, "owners": [{"id": "1832008"}], "status": "published", "stats": {"downloads": 10, "unique_downloads": 9, "views": 47, "unique_views": 47, "version_downloads": 3, "version_unique_downloads": 3, "version_unique_views": 16, "version_views": 16}, "state": "done", "submitted": true}, {"created": "2026-10-26T06:25:25.851995+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-26T06:25:26.055571+00:00", "id": 23637733, "conceptrecid": "23637732", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637732", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package for \"Evidence Contracts for Auditing Human\u2013AI Software Development: Interpreting Pull-Request Traces under Generative AI\"", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23637733", "publication_date": "2026-10-25", "description": "<p>Replication package for the article \"Evidence Contracts for Auditing Human&ndash;AI Software Development: Interpreting Pull-Request Traces under Generative AI\". An evidence contract is an executable specification of the evidence a claim about an AI-assisted pull request requires and of the signals declared insufficient for it; an interpreter returns, claim by claim, one of four verdicts (supported, not applicable, unresolved, contradicted) with a diagnosis.</p>\n<p>The package contains the contract interpreter and its tests (including exhaustive checks of four properties of the verdict semantics), every clause with its bindings, the pseudonymized snapshots of the public pull-request records used in the study (accounts replaced by truncated SHA-256 hashes, bots flagged, no comment text), the manual and AI codes of the coded samples, the scripts of the additional checks and of the stress test, and every result file used for the results reported in the article. Retrieval scripts use the GitHub CLI and need network access; the snapshots are shipped so that this step can be skipped.</p>\n<p>How to reproduce: see README.md and replication/README.md. Install the packages in replication/requirements-lock.txt (Python 3.14), run `python3 -m pytest simulation/ -q` (40 tests) and the commands listed in replication/README.md; `shasum -a 256 -c replication/SHA256SUMS` verifies every file.</p>\n<p>Not included: the coding sheets with approvers' account names, the case files with public comment text used by the AI coders, and the code of the allocation prototype from an earlier audit (its frozen outputs are kept only for the interpreter's tests). Code is released under the MIT licence; data and results under CC BY 4.0.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Pelechano, Vicente", "affiliation": "Universitat Polit\u00e8cnica de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0003-1090-230X"}, {"name": "Mestre Gascon, Antoni", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0001-8572-2579"}, {"name": "Albert Albiol, Manuela", "affiliation": "Universitat Polit\u00e8cnica de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0003-3747-400X"}, {"name": "Gil, Miriam", "affiliation": "Universitat de Val\u00e8ncia", "orcid": "0000-0002-2987-1825"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23637732"}}]}, "notes": "<p>Supports the manuscript submitted to Information and Software Technology. The two AI coders of the held-out sample are 